            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.19.0</h2>
<p>Meeting notes, rebuilt. Everything is transcribed on your Mac, faster and while you talk.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>A faster, more accurate engine on your Mac.</b> Meetings are now
      transcribed by Parakeet, which is much quicker than before and makes
      fewer mistakes in English and 24 other European languages. Whisper
      stays for everything else. <b>If you used meetings before:</b> open
      Settings → Meetings and press <i>Download</i> next to Parakeet
      (about 600 MB) — until then Jarvis keeps using Whisper.</li>
  <li><b>See the transcript while the meeting runs.</b> Open the meeting in
      Jarvis to watch lines appear as people speak. Nothing is drawn over
      your call.</li>
  <li><b>No more doubled lines on speakers.</b> When the other side leaks
      from your speakers into your mic, Jarvis no longer writes their words
      twice.</li>
  <li><b>Notes in the meeting's language.</b> A Russian meeting gets Russian
      notes.</li>
  <li><b>Record now, pause and resume.</b> Start notes without a call, and
      pause them as often as you like — nothing is recorded while paused.</li>
  <li><b>Summary templates.</b> Standup, 1:1, Sales call and Retro, besides
      the standard summary. Pick a default in Settings → Meetings, or switch
      a single meeting from its ⋯ menu.</li>
  <li><b>Keep audio (optional), re-transcribe, import.</b> Turn on
      <i>Keep audio after transcribing</i> to re-transcribe a meeting later
      with another engine or language; delete its audio any time. Import an
      audio or video file from the Meetings ⋯ menu.</li>
</ul>
<p>Audio never leaves your Mac. Only the text transcript is sent for the summary, as before.</p>
]]></description>
