        <item>
            <title>0.18.1</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:51:17 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1801</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.18.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.18.1</h2>
<p>Polish for the rule composer in Settings → Focus, all of it from looking at
the thing on screen.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Examples are on demand now.</b> Three example rules used to sit under
      the input with nothing saying what they were. They live behind
      "Show me examples" instead, grouped by what they key off — who sent it,
      what the message says, or something that happened — so you can see the
      shape of a rule before writing your own. Pick one and it drops into the
      box for you to edit.</li>
  <li><b>The input is properly aligned.</b> A single line sat pinned to the top
      of a box that was too tall for it.</li>
  <li><b>A quieter composer.</b> Smaller placeholder, smaller Add button, and
      the keyboard hint is gone — the button beside it already says what it
      does. ⌘↵ still adds.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
